## Outline Wiki API and Webhooks

**API Integration:**
Outline includes a fully featured API structured in an RPC style that enables you to programmatically interact with all aspects of Outline's data. You can use Outline's API to build everything from small automations to complete integrations.

**Webhook Support:**
Outline supports webhooks for your workspace so that an external web server can be notified by HTTP when selected events occur within Outline. As an admin you can add a new webhook through Settings → Webhooks, you can choose a descriptive name, the url to receive events, and select which events to receive.

**Webhook Features:**
- Webhooks include signature verification using HMAC-SHA256 encryption
- If a delivery fails it will be retried automatically several times with an exponential backoff, and webhooks will be automatically disabled when they have failed to deliver 25 events in a row
- All webhooks are sent as a POST request with JSON payloads containing event information and model data

**General Integration Options:**
Outline offers simple integrations into tools like Slack, Figma, and Loom, and there is also an open API available.


